the war in ukraine has come just as the  world is being threatened by a global  food supply crisis  among the worst affected countries  somalia where drought and crop failure  threaten a new famine streams of people  coming in still across you know the  dusty terrain they're carrying all their  possessions on their back they've got  kids and animals in tow they are fleeing  from the worst drought-affected areas  obviously there are a number of factors  leading to this crisis but how much is  ukraine's war  playing a role in this food prices were  already soaring due to livestock deaths  due to serial crop failures but the big  concern though is that ukraine is just  going to exacerbate this make it so much  worse the war in ukraine threatens to  turn crisis into catastrophe for  hundreds of millions globally who depend  on its grain last year its grain exports  fed 400 million people worldwide as we  filmed in ukraine last month millions of  tons are now trapped in the country it's  port stand idle  the world was already facing a food  supply crisis but russia's invasion of  ukraine is making it much much worse  with all these ukrainian ports on the  black sea now blocked the un is warning  that 47 million more people will face  acute hunger across the world if the war  goes on the latest u.n hunger report is  added afghanistan and somalia to its  list of the highest alert countries  described as facing catastrophic  conditions they're marked in red on this  map those with deteriorating conditions  include all of these countries in orange  including the democratic republic of the  congo sudan syria and kenya has just  been added to the list because of its  dependence on grain imports these  countries in yellow like sri lanka  zimbabwe angola lebanon are described as  areas of concern ukraine itself has now  been added to that list for the first  time because of what it's going through  at the hands of russia's invasion  but russia isn't bowing to mounting  international criticism let's be honest  the kremlin  is using food supplies  a stealth missile against developing  countries  russia isn't just blockading ukraine's  ports it's accused of stealing its grain  too caught on satellite loading it into  ships and the ports it's occupied  places like kenya that depend on grain  imports face soaring food prices on top  of drought and crop failure the mass  suffering caused by the war in ukraine  is being exported far beyond its borders  dominic waghorn sky news
 

